WEBVTT

1
00:00:30.583 --> 00:00:34.333
<b>In the previous verse, i.e., the twenty-first verse </b>
<b>of the fourth chapter,</b>

2
00:00:34.333 --> 00:00:39.333
<b>Lord Krishna described four qualities of an </b>
<b>advanced practitioner of Karma Yoga.</b>

3
00:00:39.333 --> 00:00:40.250
<b>Now,</b>

4
00:00:40.250 --> 00:00:46.416
<b>in this twenty-second verse, Lord Krishna is </b>
<b>describing a few more qualities of such a person.</b>

5
00:00:51.666 --> 00:00:53.541
<b>Through this verse,</b>

6
00:00:53.541 --> 00:00:58.500
<b>Lord Krishna is describing four qualities of </b>
<b>an advanced practitioner of Karma Yoga.</b>

7
00:00:58.500 --> 00:00:59.958
<b>And those qualities are:</b>

8
00:00:59.958 --> 00:01:03.208
<b>Yadṛcchā-lābha-santuṣṭaḥ,</b>

9
00:01:03.208 --> 00:01:05.166
<b>Dvandvātītaḥ,</b>

10
00:01:05.166 --> 00:01:06.416
<b>Vimatsaraḥ,</b>

11
00:01:06.416 --> 00:01:09.666
<b>Samaḥ siddhau asiddhau ca.</b>

12
00:01:09.666 --> 00:01:12.250
<b>Let's understand this.</b>

13
00:01:12.250 --> 00:01:13.458
<b>First -</b>

14
00:01:13.458 --> 00:01:16.250
<b>Yadṛcchā-lābha-santuṣṭaḥ -</b>

15
00:01:16.250 --> 00:01:20.750
<b>meaning being content with </b>
<b>whatever is obtained in life.</b>

16
00:01:20.750 --> 00:01:25.375
<b>Such a person doesn't make excessive </b>
<b>efforts for material wealth.</b>

17
00:01:25.375 --> 00:01:29.041
<b> He simply performs his every duty honestly,</b>

18
00:01:29.041 --> 00:01:35.416
<b>and is naturally satisfied with whatever </b>
<b>he gets as a result of it.</b>

19
00:01:35.416 --> 00:01:36.250
<b>Because</b>

20
00:01:36.250 --> 00:01:39.125
<b>this person is naturally content,</b>

21
00:01:39.125 --> 00:01:46.041
<b>he neither depends on anyone else nor</b>
<b>has any material expectations from others.</b>

22
00:01:46.041 --> 00:01:50.041
<b>And this is what keeps him </b>
<b>independent and peaceful.</b>

23
00:01:50.041 --> 00:01:51.416
<b>The second quality -</b>

24
00:01:51.416 --> 00:01:53.291
<b>Dvandvātītaḥ -</b>

25
00:01:53.291 --> 00:01:56.041
<b>meaning free from duality.</b>

26
00:01:56.041 --> 00:02:01.208
<b>This person knows that every </b>
<b>situation in life has two aspects,</b>

27
00:02:01.208 --> 00:02:03.208
<b>like day and night,</b>

28
00:02:03.208 --> 00:02:04.875
<b>pleasure and pain,</b>

29
00:02:04.875 --> 00:02:07.333
<b>success and failure.</b>

30
00:02:07.333 --> 00:02:11.166
<b>He knows that if one exists, the other will too,</b>

31
00:02:11.166 --> 00:02:15.791
<b>and he accepts both these aspects with ease.</b>

32
00:02:15.791 --> 00:02:20.250
<b>This is what keeps him balanced </b>
<b>even in difficult circumstances.</b>

33
00:02:20.250 --> 00:02:21.458
<b>The third quality -</b>

34
00:02:21.458 --> 00:02:22.791
<b>Vimatsaraḥ -</b>

35
00:02:22.791 --> 00:02:25.916
<b>meaning free from envy.</b>

36
00:02:25.916 --> 00:02:30.375
<b>The root cause of envy is </b>
<b>dissatisfaction with one's own life.</b>

37
00:02:30.375 --> 00:02:35.416
<b>Because it is in that situation that a </b>
<b>person compares his life with others'.</b>

38
00:02:35.416 --> 00:02:36.250
<b>But</b>

39
00:02:36.250 --> 00:02:40.250
<b>a spiritually advanced person remains content</b>

40
00:02:40.250 --> 00:02:46.333
<b>and accepts both good and bad circumstances </b>
<b>as an integral part of life.</b>

41
00:02:46.333 --> 00:02:47.250
<b>For this reason,</b>

42
00:02:47.250 --> 00:02:49.416
<b>he doesn't envy others;</b>

43
00:02:49.416 --> 00:02:53.666
<b>rather, he is happy in others' progress.</b>

44
00:02:53.666 --> 00:02:59.708
<b>This is what generates inner peace in him.</b>

45
00:02:59.708 --> 00:03:01.208
<b>The fourth quality</b>

46
00:03:01.208 --> 00:03:04.291
<b>(Samaḥ siddhau asiddhau ca) –</b>

47
00:03:04.291 --> 00:03:10.166
<b>meaning remaining equally steady</b>
<b>in both success and failure.</b>

48
00:03:10.166 --> 00:03:12.000
<b>It is essential to understand this.</b>

49
00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:16.208
<b>Because it's not just that he </b>
<b>doesn't get sad in failure,</b>

50
00:03:16.208 --> 00:03:19.666
<b>he also doesn't feel excessive elation in success.</b>

51
00:03:19.666 --> 00:03:24.916
<b>He knows that success and failure </b>
<b>don't depend only on him.</b>

52
00:03:24.916 --> 00:03:32.000
<b>Success and failure also have the hand of </b>
<b>circumstances, other people, his past actions.</b>

53
00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:35.916
<b>Then why excessive sorrow, </b>
<b>and why excessive elation?</b>

54
00:03:35.916 --> 00:03:40.791
<b>And this very thought keeps him steady</b>
<b>in the ups and downs of life.</b>

55
00:03:40.791 --> 00:03:44.500
<b>Understand this with the example of a student.</b>

56
00:03:44.500 --> 00:03:47.875
<b>For an exam, what is in a student's hands?</b>

57
00:03:47.875 --> 00:03:49.500
<b>Only his hard work.</b>

58
00:03:49.500 --> 00:03:52.500
<b>Will there be any benefit in </b>
<b>comparing with others?</b>

59
00:03:52.500 --> 00:03:53.333
<b>No.</b>

60
00:03:53.333 --> 00:03:56.625
<b>If he gets proud of being better than others,</b>

61
00:03:56.625 --> 00:03:58.666
<b>his hard work will decrease.</b>

62
00:03:58.666 --> 00:04:01.500
<b>If he grieves over being behind others,</b>

63
00:04:01.500 --> 00:04:03.750
<b>his self-confidence will diminish.</b>

64
00:04:03.750 --> 00:04:10.583
<b>And moreover, it is the law of nature that in </b>
<b>marks, someone will be ahead, someone behind.</b>

65
00:04:10.583 --> 00:04:16.666
<b>So, it is appropriate that he works hard, </b>
<b>and then accepts whatever result comes.</b>

66
00:04:16.666 --> 00:04:22.083
<b>And then learning from the result, he should</b>
<b>get engrossed in studying for the next exam.</b>

67
00:04:22.083 --> 00:04:25.250
<b>This was a practical example,</b>

68
00:04:25.250 --> 00:04:26.000
<b>but</b>

69
00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:29.833
<b>the person who is endowed with the </b>
<b>spiritual knowledge of Karma Yoga</b>

70
00:04:29.833 --> 00:04:37.291
<b>knows that good or bad, he remains grateful </b>
<b>considering every result as God's blessing</b>

71
00:04:37.291 --> 00:04:41.041
<b>and performs his duties.</b>

72
00:04:45.583 --> 00:04:47.708
<b>Vimatsaraḥ -</b>

73
00:04:47.708 --> 00:04:49.208
<b>meaning</b>

74
00:04:49.208 --> 00:04:52.083
<b>free from envy.</b>

75
00:04:52.083 --> 00:04:56.666
<b>This is extremely necessary for personal life.</b>

76
00:04:56.666 --> 00:04:57.875
<b>Envy</b>

77
00:04:57.875 --> 00:05:00.041
<b>is a negative emotion</b>

78
00:05:00.041 --> 00:05:05.708
<b>that arises when you compare yourself to others</b>

79
00:05:05.708 --> 00:05:09.541
<b>and consider your situation inferior to theirs.</b>

80
00:05:09.541 --> 00:05:16.125
<b>And this very envy generates </b>
<b>dissatisfaction and stress.</b>

81
00:05:16.125 --> 00:05:22.125
<b>It is necessary to avoid envy because </b>
<b>it distorts your thinking.</b>

82
00:05:22.125 --> 00:05:26.666
<b>Instead of taking inspiration from </b>
<b>someone's successes and virtues,</b>

83
00:05:26.666 --> 00:05:31.000
<b>it awakens animosity towards them in you.</b>

84
00:05:31.000 --> 00:05:32.500
<b>Think,</b>

85
00:05:32.500 --> 00:05:37.333
<b>how detrimental this is to your progress.</b>

86
00:05:37.333 --> 00:05:47.458
<b>To avoid this harmful tendency, understand </b>
<b>and follow these four practical measures.</b>

87
00:05:47.458 --> 00:05:49.083
<b>First -</b>

88
00:05:49.083 --> 00:05:52.166
<b>Practice gratitude –</b>

89
00:05:52.166 --> 00:05:54.291
<b>Look around you,</b>

90
00:05:54.291 --> 00:05:59.333
<b>you have received a lot in life. Appreciate it.</b>

91
00:05:59.333 --> 00:06:00.750
<b>Second -</b>

92
00:06:00.750 --> 00:06:04.041
<b>Focus on personal progress –</b>

93
00:06:04.041 --> 00:06:05.041
<b>Think,</b>

94
00:06:05.041 --> 00:06:13.083
<b>if you keep focusing on others' lives and their </b>
<b>progress instead of focusing on your goal,</b>

95
00:06:13.083 --> 00:06:16.833
<b>it will only slow down your own pace.</b>

96
00:06:16.833 --> 00:06:17.958
<b>Third -</b>

97
00:06:17.958 --> 00:06:22.000
<b>Practice being happy in others' success –</b>

98
00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:25.000
<b>Transform envy into genuine appreciation.</b>

99
00:06:25.000 --> 00:06:31.333
<b>This will also encourage you to take </b>
<b>positive lessons from someone else's success.</b>

100
00:06:31.333 --> 00:06:33.000
<b>The fourth measure –</b>

101
00:06:33.000 --> 00:06:36.583
<b>Introspect and be aware –</b>

102
00:06:36.583 --> 00:06:38.083
<b>Remember,</b>

103
00:06:38.083 --> 00:06:41.291
<b>you are on the path of spiritual progress,</b>

104
00:06:41.291 --> 00:06:44.958
<b>some things will change only slowly.</b>

105
00:06:44.958 --> 00:06:45.750
<b>So</b>

106
00:06:45.750 --> 00:06:54.916
<b>even if you experience envy, don't berate yourself </b>
<b>– just understand that experience.</b>

107
00:06:54.916 --> 00:06:57.583
<b>Why did envy arise in you?</b>

108
00:06:57.583 --> 00:07:02.791
<b>And this very awareness will lead</b>
<b>you on the right path.</b>

109
00:07:02.791 --> 00:07:07.666
<b>Freedom from envy will focus</b>
<b>you towards your goals.</b>

110
00:07:07.666 --> 00:07:12.166
<b>It will give you lasting contentment </b>
<b>and inner peace.</b>

111
00:07:12.166 --> 00:07:18.208
<b>Keep this in mind and stay away from envy.</b>

112
00:07:22.333 --> 00:07:25.000
<b>Dvandvātītaḥ</b>

113
00:07:25.000 --> 00:07:30.291
<b>meaning freedom from duality.</b>

114
00:07:30.291 --> 00:07:37.875
<b>It is necessary to understand that every</b>
<b>situation in life has two aspects,</b>

115
00:07:37.875 --> 00:07:45.041
<b>like day and night, pleasure and pain.</b>

116
00:07:45.041 --> 00:07:46.458
<b>Similarly,</b>

117
00:07:46.458 --> 00:07:50.750
<b>there is this duality in humans too,</b>

118
00:07:50.750 --> 00:07:52.166
<b>two aspects,</b>

119
00:07:52.166 --> 00:07:54.833
<b>two types of habits,</b>

120
00:07:54.833 --> 00:08:05.375
<b>some that will match your</b>
<b>thoughts, some that won't.</b>

121
00:08:05.375 --> 00:08:14.166
<b>Being free from this good/bad duality </b>
<b>makes family and social life smooth.</b>

122
00:08:14.166 --> 00:08:23.708
<b>When you start to believe that both you </b>
<b>and others have right/wrong aspects,</b>

123
00:08:23.708 --> 00:08:27.750
<b>it will mature relationships.</b>

124
00:08:27.750 --> 00:08:33.125
<b>In such a case, you appreciate others' goodness,</b>

125
00:08:33.125 --> 00:08:34.541
<b>but</b>

126
00:08:34.541 --> 00:08:38.750
<b>you don't get disturbed if some mistake happens.</b>

127
00:08:38.750 --> 00:08:42.041
<b>Because you know</b>

128
00:08:42.041 --> 00:08:50.083
<b>that even a good person making a mistake</b>
<b>is a natural duality of life.</b>

129
00:08:50.083 --> 00:08:51.333
<b>Also,</b>

130
00:08:51.333 --> 00:08:59.375
<b> this means that you know that no </b>
<b>one becomes bad intentionally,</b>

131
00:08:59.375 --> 00:09:02.458
<b>they must have had some circumstances.</b>

132
00:09:02.458 --> 00:09:09.041
<b>If circumstances are bad today, they will </b>
<b>also change and become good tomorrow.</b>

133
00:09:09.041 --> 00:09:15.583
<b>Understand the duality of life, </b>
<b>and try to remain free from it.</b>

134
00:09:15.583 --> 00:09:21.750
<b>Practice the feeling of equanimity in</b>
<b>both good and bad circumstances.</b>

135
00:09:26.583 --> 00:09:28.791
<b>Envy,</b>

136
00:09:28.791 --> 00:09:34.541
<b>it only brings harm in the professional setting.</b>

137
00:09:34.541 --> 00:09:38.375
<b>Envy awakens</b>

138
00:09:38.375 --> 00:09:43.666
<b>when you compare your professional </b>
<b>progress or achievements</b>

139
00:09:43.666 --> 00:09:49.541
<b>with your colleagues or someone else.</b>

140
00:09:49.541 --> 00:09:53.458
<b>This comparison will not </b>
<b>only give you dissatisfaction</b>

141
00:09:53.458 --> 00:10:00.625
<b>but also injects poison in the </b>
<b>professional environment.</b>

142
00:10:00.625 --> 00:10:08.791
<b>Due to envy, a person often forgets </b>
<b>his own and the organization's progress</b>

143
00:10:08.791 --> 00:10:13.625
<b>and starts thinking of ways to </b>
<b>hinder others' progress,</b>

144
00:10:13.625 --> 00:10:17.708
<b>tries to push others back.</b>

145
00:10:17.708 --> 00:10:25.375
<b>This does not benefit anyone, </b>
<b>neither you nor the organization.</b>

146
00:10:25.375 --> 00:10:33.458
<b>For professional progress, instead </b>
<b>of focusing on others, focus on your goals,</b>

147
00:10:33.458 --> 00:10:36.291
<b>have faith in your hard work.</b>

148
00:10:36.291 --> 00:10:42.000
<b>Yes, competition is natural in</b>
<b>professional organizations,</b>

149
00:10:42.000 --> 00:10:45.208
<b>it will also benefit the organization.</b>

150
00:10:45.208 --> 00:10:46.416
<b>But</b>

151
00:10:46.416 --> 00:10:53.708
<b>if the competition becomes unbalanced, </b>
<b>it can be harmful.</b>

152
00:10:53.708 --> 00:10:59.458
<b>Understand the difference between </b>
<b>envy and healthy competition.</b>

153
00:10:59.458 --> 00:11:05.041
<b>Competition in balanced measure - is positive.</b>

154
00:11:05.041 --> 00:11:10.041
<b>Envy - is completely negative</b>

155
00:11:10.041 --> 00:11:12.291
<b>Maintain healthy competition,</b>

156
00:11:12.291 --> 00:11:13.333
<b>but</b>

157
00:11:13.333 --> 00:11:17.583
<b>always stay away from envy.</b>

